clan":"sase-1p1","agent_clan_generation":"20261027152404","agent_session":"sase-1p1.1","agent_session_role":"plan","bead_id":"sase-1p1.1","changespec_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","cl_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","clan_summary":"[bold #D75FFF]◆ EPIC sase-1p1[/bold #D75FFF]\n[dim]  Title: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]Footprint: a local usage census for finding what sase should delete[/bold #D7AFFF]\n[dim]   Goal: [#D7D7AF][/dim]sase keeps an always-on, privacy-by-construction census of which of[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]its surfaces (CLI commands and options, TUI actions and keys, views[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]and modals, macros, skills, config leaves, automation) are used, by[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]whom, and how. The census costs at most one appended line per CLI [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]process and one in-memory counter bump per TUI action. A Statistics[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]→ Footprint view and a `sase footprint` command turn it into a [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]review workflow that ends in keep reasons and deletion task beads. [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]The local data contains only allowlisted IDs and enum values, so it[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]can later be exported, and export packs carry no identity.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]13[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]8[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202610/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]footprint_usage_census.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202610/footprint_usage_census.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-1p1[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-1p1/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Feature catalog, ID scheme, overlay, and drift guard[/bold #D7AFFF]          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog: create the stdlib-only footprint package foundation (ids, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]paths), the generator that walks every sase registry into a checked-in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog.jsonl, the protected/keep overlay, the sync tool wired into just[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]fix/lint, and `sase footprint catalog`.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Rust ledger, spool fold, and status (sase-core)[/bold #D7AFFF]               [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]ledger[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]ledger: add the sase-core `footprint` domain (spool line validation, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog ingest, checkpointed fold into the daily ledger, coverage, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]derived-row upsert, status, prune, clear), its PyO3 bindings, the Python[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]facade, and the CI pin move.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]CLI recorder, spool writer, and mode switch[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]cli_recording[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]cli_recording: record one spool line per CLI process from a single [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]try/finally in entry.py (fast paths, help, usage errors, cancels, option[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]dest names), classify the actor from env markers, add `sase footprint [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mode`, exclude pytest, and prove the 100 µs budget.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]TUI counters, dispatch seams, and flush thread[/bold #D7AFFF]                [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui_recording[dim] · [dim][/dim]after cli_recording[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui_reco